    "mainEntity": [
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "How do I create a GST invoice online for free?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "Open ihatepdf.cv/gst-invoice, enter your business details, your customer's details and the line items. CGST, SGST and IGST are calculated automatically based on whether the supply is intra-state or inter-state, an HSN/SAC summary is generated, and you download a compliant Tax Invoice as a PDF. Free, no account, no subscription, and your billing data never leaves your device."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "What must a GST tax invoice legally contain?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "Under the CGST Rules an invoice needs: the supplier's name, address and GSTIN; a consecutive serial number for the financial year; the date of issue; the recipient's name, address and GSTIN where registered; the HSN or SAC code; a description, quantity and taxable value for each item; the rate and amount of CGST, SGST, IGST or cess; the place of supply; whether tax is payable on reverse charge; and a signature or digital signature. The generator prompts for each of these."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "When do I charge CGST and SGST instead of IGST?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "It depends on the place of supply. If the supplier and the place of supply are in the same state, the tax splits into CGST and SGST at half the total rate each. If they are in different states — or the supply is an export or to an SEZ — IGST applies at the full rate. Entering the correct state on both sides makes the tool apply the right split automatically."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "Is a GSTIN validated?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "The format is checked — 15 characters, with the first two digits being the state code, ten characters of PAN, an entity number, a fixed letter and a check digit. That catches typos and transposed characters. It confirms the number is well-formed, not that it is currently active, so verify status on the GST portal for a new customer."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "Do I need to include HSN codes?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "It depends on turnover. Businesses above the prescribed turnover threshold must report HSN codes for goods and SAC codes for services, at either four or six digits depending on the slab. The generator produces an HSN/SAC summary table alongside the invoice."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "Can I use this for a bill of supply or a composition scheme?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "A composition dealer cannot collect GST and must issue a Bill of Supply rather than a Tax Invoice, with the prescribed declaration instead of a tax breakdown. This tool generates a Tax Invoice, so it fits a regular registered supplier; a composition dealer should adapt the output accordingly."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "Is my invoice and customer data stored anywhere?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "No. Everything runs in your browser and nothing is transmitted or retained on any server. There is no account, so there is no database holding your customer list, your turnover or your invoice history."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "Is this the same as e-invoicing on the IRP?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "No, and the distinction matters. E-invoicing requires businesses above the notified turnover threshold to report invoices to the Invoice Registration Portal and obtain an IRN and signed QR code. This tool produces a compliant printed Tax Invoice document; it does not register invoices with the IRP. If you are within the e-invoicing mandate you must also report through the portal."
