        <p style="font-size:0.875rem;color:#a1a1aa;line-height:1.75;margin:0">An invoice contains your GSTIN, your customer's GSTIN, your prices, your margins and a running picture of your turnover. Handing that to a free cloud invoicing service means an unfamiliar company holds a complete commercial record of your business, and free tiers are usually free because that data has value. Here nothing is transmitted and nothing is stored on a server; the invoice is assembled and rendered in your browser and downloaded to your machine. There is no account to lose access to, no subscription to lapse at an inconvenient moment, and no vendor holding your billing history hostage.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="margin-top:28px">
        <h2 style="font-size:1.05rem;font-weight:700;color:#fff;margin:0 0 10px">GST invoice requirements in India</h2>
        <p style="font-size:0.875rem;color:#a1a1aa;line-height:1.75;margin:0">A valid GST tax invoice must include: the supplier's name, address, and GSTIN; the invoice number and date; the recipient's name, address, and GSTIN (for B2B transactions); a description of goods or services with HSN/SAC codes; quantity and value; the applicable GST rate and tax amount (CGST + SGST for intra-state, IGST for inter-state); and the total invoice value. ihatepdf's GST Invoice Generator includes all mandatory fields and calculates all tax amounts automatically.</p>
