          <h3 style="font-size:0.925rem;font-weight:600;color:#e4e4e7;margin:0 0 5px">Is this the same as e-invoicing on the IRP?</h3>
          <p style="font-size:0.875rem;color:#a1a1aa;margin:0;line-height:1.65">No, and the distinction matters. E-invoicing requires businesses above the notified turnover threshold to report invoices to the Invoice Registration Portal and obtain an IRN and signed QR code. This tool produces a compliant printed Tax Invoice document; it does not register invoices with the IRP. If you are within the e-invoicing mandate you must also report through the portal.</p>
